  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Mozambique 2025 &#x2013; UNICEF Cholera Coordinator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF&#x2019;s cholera programme scaled up significantly in 2023 following the largest outbreak on record in the country. The situation in early 2024 was more mild due to limited rains/drought. However, as we near the end of 2024 the situation has escalated significant. In Nametil, Mogovolas, the outbreak has been surging for months. The situation is complicated by mistrust, rumors and the dynamic political context related to the upcoming election results announcements. UNICEF also has several provinces where cholera is confirmed but the government will not declare and official outbreak. Additional support is required to provide technical support to the &#x201c;cholera cell&#x201d; made up of a disciplinary team of health, wash and (SBC) Science Behaviour Change colleagues under the supervision of the Chief of Field Operations/Emergencies.</narrative>
  </description>
